  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
>
  <article class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <ArticleHeader kicker={"Buyer's Guide"} badge={"Label-Checked"} author={author} dates={dates} mobileAd={false}>
      <Fragment slot="title">Best Salted Caramel Protein Powder</Fragment>
      Seven salted caramel powders checked against the label for that flavor, with the sodium, sweetener and caramel ingredients spelled out so you know what you are paying for.
    </ArticleHeader>

    <TableOfContents>
      <a href="#compared">Compared at a Glance</a>
      <a href="#whats-inside">What Makes Salted Caramel</a>
      <a href="#top-picks">Our Top Picks</a>
      <a href="#flavor-numbers">Sodium and Other Numbers</a>
      <a href="#sweeteners">Sweeteners</a>
      <a href="#coffee">Salted Caramel in Coffee</a>
      <a href="#recipes">Recipes and Uses</a>
      <a href="#buyer-feedback">What Buyers Say</a>
      <a href="#mistakes">Common Mistakes</a>
      <a href="#faq">FAQ</a>
    </TableOfContents>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="lede">
          Salted caramel is a coffee-shop flavor that protein brands have learned to copy well, and it has two quirks the labels reveal. The salt is real, so salted caramel tubs often carry noticeably more sodium than the same brand's other flavors, and the caramel is almost always flavoring rather than cooked sugar, which keeps sugar near zero. For most people, Dymatize ISO100 Salted Caramel is the best pick: 25 g of protein, 110 calories and 1 g of sugar per scoop, per Dymatize's label at the time of writing. The rest of this guide covers the higher-protein, stevia-sweetened, budget and plant-based alternatives.
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />

        <div id="compared" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. Salted Caramel Protein Powder Compared at a Glance
          </h2>

          <p>
            All seven picks side by side. Protein and calories are per labeled serving, which is one scoop for the whey powders and two scoops for KOS. Where a brand does not publish a full panel for this flavor, the figures come from retailer or nutrition database copies of the label and are marked as approximate.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="w-full text-left">
                <thead class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-200">
