                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Product</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Protein/scoop</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Calories</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Sugar</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Price tier</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Certification</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Dymatize ISO100 Salted Caramel</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">25 g</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">110</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">1 g</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Premium</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Informed Choice (brand)</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Quest Protein Powder Salted Caramel</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">26 g</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">120</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">1 g</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Premium</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">None found</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Legion Whey+ Salted Caramel</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">About 22 g</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">About 120</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Check label</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Premium</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Labdoor tested (brand)</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Transparent Labs Isolate Salted Chocolate Caramel</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">About 28 g</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">About 130</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Check label</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Premium</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Informed Choice (brand)</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Nutricost Whey Isolate Salted Caramel</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">30 g</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">About 120-140</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Check label</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Budget</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">None confirmed</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Myprotein Impact Whey Isolate Salted Caramel</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">About 21-25 g</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">About 90-110</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Check label</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Mid</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Informed Choice (UK listings)</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">KOS Organic Plant Protein Salted Caramel Coffee</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">20 g (2 scoops)</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">About 150-160</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Check label</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Mid</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">NSF listing at a retailer; confirm seal</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>

          <p>
            The headline differences are protein per scoop and price. Nutricost gives the most protein per serving at 30 g and is the cheapest per gram, but with less certification to back it. ISO100 and Quest are the best-documented, with full panels on their own product pages. Transparent Labs and Legion are the stevia-sweetened options for buyers avoiding sucralose. KOS is the only dairy-free pick, and it contains caffeine.
          </p>

          <p>
            One number the table leaves out is sodium, which matters more for this flavor than any other. ISO100 Salted Caramel lists 190 mg per scoop and Quest lists 310 mg, both higher than their other flavors. The section on sodium below explains the gap and why it matters if you drink two or three shakes a day.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="whats-inside" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            2. What Makes Salted Caramel Protein Powder Taste Like Caramel?
          </h2>

          <p>
            Real caramel is sugar cooked until it browns, and no protein powder here contains much of it. Instead, the caramel taste comes from flavor compounds listed as natural flavors or natural and artificial flavors, which recreate the buttery, toasted notes of cooked sugar without the carbohydrate. Dymatize ISO100 Salted Caramel lists natural and artificial flavor, salt, soy lecithin, sucralose and stevia alongside its two whey isolates, and its panel shows 1 g of sugar with 0 g added.
          </p>

          <p>
            Quest adds small amounts of molasses and sugar to its salted caramel for depth, but the label says they contribute only a trivial amount of added sugar, and the panel shows 1 g of total sugar and 0 g added per scoop. Transparent Labs' salted chocolate caramel combines cocoa with caramel flavor, which makes it closer to a chocolate caramel candy than a pure salted caramel. KOS pairs caramel flavor with organic coffee and a little coconut sugar, so its profile is closer to a salted caramel latte.
          </p>

          <p>
            The salt is real. Sea salt or salt appears on every salted caramel label we checked, and it does real flavor work: a small amount of salt sharpens sweetness and suppresses bitterness, which is why salted caramel can taste less artificial than plain caramel. It also explains the higher sodium figures, which we cover in the next section after the product cards.
          </p>

          <p>
            Caramel color is a separate ingredient and is not the same as caramel flavor. It is a brown colorant made by heating sugars, sometimes with ammonia or sulfite compounds, and some classes can contain a by-product called 4-MEI, which California lists under Proposition 65. None of the ingredient lists we checked for ISO100, Quest, Transparent Labs or Nutricost salted caramel include caramel color, but it does appear in some other caramel-flavored foods and drinks. If you want to avoid it, read the ingredient list rather than assuming a brown powder contains it.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8 my-8">
            <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#38BDF8] mb-3">LABEL TIP</p>
            <p class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-3">Caramel flavor is not caramel color</p>
