            9. Common Mistakes to Avoid
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Ignoring the sodium line</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Salted caramel often carries more sodium than other flavors. Quest lists 310 mg per scoop, about double its cookies and cream. One scoop is fine for most people, but two or three a day on a salty diet adds up, especially with high blood pressure.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Confusing caramel flavor with caramel color</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Caramel flavor adds taste and is listed as natural or artificial flavor. Caramel color is a separate brown colorant listed by name. None of the salted caramel labels we checked use it, but do not assume either way. Read the ingredient list.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Stacking caffeine without noticing</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                KOS Salted Caramel Coffee contains about 50 mg of caffeine per serving. Adding it to a cup of coffee or taking it with a pre-workout raises your total quickly. Count it alongside your other caffeine sources, especially later in the day.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Dumping powder into hot coffee</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Whey clumps when dry powder hits very hot liquid. Mix the scoop with a little cool milk first, then add coffee that has cooled for a minute or two, or use an iced latte method. A handheld frother makes a smooth drink.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Assuming the numbers match the brand's best-seller</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Flavors change protein, calories and sodium. ISO100 Salted Caramel has 110 calories against 120 for its cookies and cream, and Myprotein's labels differ by market. Always read the panel for salted caramel on the tub in your hand.
              </p>
            </div>
